bucket resources into projects and place max/min restrictions on them. later assign users to this project.

had to use this to leash the Java threads during development stage that were taking up 100% of cpu.

commands are projadd / projmod or better yet use capctl after projadd to add and control. 

to use the cpu-shares option you ll have to change dispadmin -d FSS since shares only make sense in FSS scheduling
but you can always use cpu-cap. 50% means 50% of one cpu whereas 150% means 100% of one cpu and 50% of the other cpu.

